# The rule surface is governed by `npm run check:load`, a byte ratchet on what an agent loads before
# reading code — not by table aesthetics. Prettier pads every markdown table to its widest cell, which
# costs 4,066 B across the instructions (+2,802 B in project-workflow's gate table alone) and 2,336 B
# across the agents, and buys nothing: the padding is invisible to a reader and is charged to every
# scoped task. These two directories are the only `.github/` paths prettier would change today, so
# they are formatted by hand and measured, never reformatted: padding here would move the ratchet.
# `.github/copilot-instructions.md` and `.github/AGENTS.md` sit in the same ratchet but are already
# clean, so they stay checked — keep them clean by hand. `format:check:changed` stays vacuous for the
# two ignored directories by design; `format:check` is the gate that covers the rest of `.github/`.
.github/agents/**
.github/instructions/**
